  "description": "Demolition of existing rear conservatory and erection of a single storey rear extension; elevational alterations comprising replacement windows, insertion of clerestory windows to front, enlargement of window to rear, enlargement of front door, removal of front steps; landscaping alterations; erection of bin and bike store to front garden.&nbsp;",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "<p>All new external facing and roofing materials in respect of all the works hereby approved (and any other incidental works carried out in this connection) shall match those of the existing building in respect of materials used, detailed execution and finished appearance including type, size, colour, bond, pointing, coursing, jointing, profile and texture (delete as appropriate)</p><p><br></p><p>REASON: To ensure the development integrates with the host building and surrounding area.</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;Prior to superstructure works, detailed specification, a drainage layout and a management &amp;amp; maintenance plan (where applicable) of the proposed rainwater SuDS planter, rain garden, water butt, permeable paving and green roof shall be submitted to, and approved by the LPA, in consultation with the LLFA. If soakaways i.e. plastic modules and soakaway rings are used, an infiltration test must be carried out to ensure that the capacity of the soil is suitable for infiltration. It must be demonstrated that there will be no increase in surface water flow being discharged offsite and an overall reduction in peak flow rate and volume.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;REASON: To promote sustainable water management and prevent increased surface water runoff into the local network.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
